SUMMARY:In Search of Home
DESCRIPTION:Lucknow is no longer quite the city it once was: a place of old-world grace\, Urdu poetry\, and tehzeeb\, now reshaped by market capitalism and communalism. This conversation\, centred on the novella Homecoming\, explores what it means for India to undergo one of the largest urbanisations in history. With cities and culture morphing into unrecognisable\, and sometimes alienating\, new forms\, what makes a space worth belonging to? \nBeyond the novel lies a larger question of language tied to belonging: how lived experience is shaped by the language spoken in a place\, a thread the author has long explored. The conversation will also examine the exchange between author and reader\, asking what spaces writing can leave for imagination to fill. \nVenue: Library\n\n\nOn Love\, Memory and Belonging in a Changing City\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfwxaWCncQk0nrQuvLEC-U2joM0QITingGbB3ADkKZkZH_e6A/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Speakers*: Omair Ahmad\, Sumana Mukherjee\n*Event Categories*: Books\, Cities\, Culture\, Language\, Poetry\, Society
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/in-search-of-home/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Books,Cities,Culture,Language,Poetry,Society
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Thumbnailsep19h.jpg
