SUMMARY:Fire Drawing Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever played with fire? \nIn this hands-on workshop participants learn a technique the artist has spent five years developing: burning or “fuming” wood with matches\, candles\, and pyrography tools to create textured\, tonal\, almost painterly images. The process allows partial control over the outcome\, producing fine relief-like details and layered effects akin to glazing with flame. \nFire is at the heart of creation\, alongside wood and the artist’s own hands\, in a slow\, attentive dialogue between intention and element. Participants will experiment directly with flame and wood\, exploring a completely new material language while reconnecting with something older: attentiveness to matter\, to process\, and to the natural world. \nPlease Note: Limited to 50 seats. Children 6+ are welcome to attend\, provided they are accompanied by a parent or caregiver. \nVenue: Gallery\n\n\nFire as an Elemental Drawing of Shared Ecologies\nRSVPs closed. Thank you for your interest.\n*Facilitator*: Arta Raituma\n*Event Categories*: Visual Arts\, Workshops
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/fire-drawing-workshop/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Visual Arts,Workshops
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Thumbnail-6.jpg
