SUMMARY:India after Bhagat Singh
DESCRIPTION:Language: Hindi\, Urdu\, and English \nWhat happened to the fierce romanticism of Bhagat Singh’s revolutionary spirit? \nThis solo play explores the profound changes the nation has undergone since the martyrdom of the legendary freedom fighter. Breathing new life into his revolutionary philosophy\, the performance holds his core ideals of justice\, equality\, and freedom\, up against modern-day socio-political scenarios. \nThe soil of Jallianwala Bagh\, the site of the massacre that revolutionised young Bhagat Singh\, is not merely dirt preserved in an urn. It is a witness to systemic cruelty\, unheeded cries\, and human sacrifice. When destruction and violence unfold today\, in Manipur\, Kashmir\, or the Hasdeo forests\, the same soil bleeds again. The play asks: how many unrecognised Jallianwala Baghs must exist before humanity notices? Both a mirror to contemporary society and an urgent call to remember the true spirit of the nation’s struggle\, this performance refuses to let history stay history. \n\nSupported by:\n\n\nVenue: Auditorium\n\n\n\n\nRevisiting an Ideology in a Changing India\nFor Ages 10+\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdP16f6mBHmqiGsC420DKNUJhd4UbT2N1TR2CUhy265Kcktdw/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Performer*: Shubham Tiwari\n*Event Categories*: Performing Arts\, Theatre
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/india-after-bhagat-singh/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Performing Arts,Theatre
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Thumbnail-8.jpg
END:VEVENT
