SUMMARY:Shera
DESCRIPTION:\n20 min | Kumaoni with English subtitles \nAll Monu can think about as he roams the forests with his best friend Raju\, is spotting the elusive leopard\, Shera\, before his family moves away to the city. Time is running out\, so Raju comes up with an idea: a little dangerous\, but maybe just crazy enough to work. Will they find Shera in time? \nWatch the film\, flip through the beautifully illustrated graphic book\, and meet the storyteller behind it all! Shera began as a short film and grew into a graphic book\, hand-painted by acclaimed artist Allen Shaw\, bringing to life the magic and mystery of the Himalayan valleys of Kumaon. Beyond the adventure lies a story about home\, moving away\, and a community learning to share its world with a wild\, wonderful neighbour. \n\nAround the World in 50 Sundays is a journey that begins\, not with a ticket\, but with opening a book. In a city like Bangalore where families are always in motion\, the BIC Library hopes to offer stillness and a quiet\, welcoming space for both parents and children where reading becomes a shared experience. Every Sunday\, we open our doors to invite you into a library that listens; building a rhythm of return\, a habit of joy and a new community bound not just by books\, but by the weekly ritual of reading together.\n\nWe welcome your ideas and input. If you have suggestions for children’s events or activities that align with this vision\, we’d love to hear from you. Please reach out to us at library@bangaloreinternationalcentre.org \nSupported by:\n \nVenue: Library\n\n\n\n\nReady for an Adventure in the Mountains?\nFor Ages 8-12\nRSVPs will open Mon\, Sep 21 at 6pm.\n*Facilitator*: Arun Fulara\n*Event Categories*: Around the World in 50 Sundays
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/shera/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Around the World in 50 Sundays
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Thumbnail_WSOC.jpg
END:VEVENT
