SUMMARY:Songs of the Seeker
DESCRIPTION:This musical concert is inspired by the poetry and philosophy of the 15th-century mystic poet\, Saint Kabir. Original compositions and reimagined bhajans carry Kabir’s timeless words into a new sonic world\, where folk instruments and Indian melodic traditions meet electronic textures\, vocal harmonies\, and unexpected percussion. \nEveryday objects become instruments\, and familiar sounds take on new forms\, as the performance drifts between stillness and groove\, meditation and momentum. Audiences are invited to listen\, reflect\, and sing along\, becoming seekers themselves for an evening. \nThe Sadho Project\nThe ensemble is a Bengaluru-based quintet reimagining Indian sound through electronic innovation\, blending traditional motifs\, field textures\, and ambient layers. Their music unfolds where the pulse of machines meets the soul of melody\, creating space for reflection and transformation. \nSupported by:\n \nVenue: Auditorium\n\n\nImmersive Experimental Music Exploring Kabirdas’ Poetry\nRSVPs will open Fri\, Sep 25 at 6pm.\n*Performers*: Vivaswath Rao\, Roopini Ravindran\, Kusumitha Vasanth\, Aditi Bharatee\, Anirudh Sharma\n*Event Categories*: Music\, Performing Arts\, Philosophy
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/songs-of-the-seeker/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Music,Performing Arts,Philosophy
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Thumbnail_SOTS.jpg
END:VEVENT
